<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Mascouten</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Mascouten were an Algonquian-speaking people of the western <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-lakes">Great Lakes</a> region, known to the French as the 'Fire Nation'. In the 17th century they were at war with the Neutral and other Iroquoian peoples and later lived in present-day <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/wisconsin">Wisconsin</a>. Weakened by war and disease, they merged in the 18th century with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kickapoo">Kickapoo</a> and other neighbours and disappeared as a separate people.</p></div>
